@startuml fig_embedded_vs_normalized
!include _style.puml
' Book figure — normalized child rows vs a bounded child collection inside the parent.
' Form: structure. Evidence status: conceptual illustration; asserts no rate.
title normalized child rows vs an embedded bounded collection
top to bottom direction
skinparam nodesep 16
skinparam ranksep 24

rectangle "normalized — many independent child rows" as N #FBFBF6 {
  rectangle "Donor\ndonor_id · display_name" as ND <<authoritative>>
  rectangle "Donation\ndonation_id · donor_id · amount" as ND2 <<authoritative>>
  ND --> ND2 : has many
}
note bottom of ND2
  Reading the whole aggregate needs the parent
  and its children; each child is queryable and
  updatable on its own.
end note

rectangle "embedded — the child collection lives in the parent row" as E #FBFBF6 {
  rectangle "Donor\ndonor_id · display_name\ndonations: [ { donation_id, amount }, … ]" as ED <<authoritative>>
}
note bottom of ED
  Reading the whole bounded aggregate is local to
  one row; querying or updating one independent
  child is less convenient, and an unbounded
  collection is dangerous.
end note

ND2 -[hidden]right-> ED
@enduml
